The code in examples/ and in docs/MODDING.md is free to use as you like, with no credit needed.

Not allowed without asking first: reuploading Chef Shared Loader (anywhere, in any form), or releasing the loader, or
most of it, under another name as your own loader.

Continuing the loader: if no new version of Chef Shared Loader has been released on this repository's GitHub
Releases page for 3 months in a row, you may ask to continue it. Open an issue on this repository saying what you
plan. If within 30 days I haven't released a new version or said in that issue that I'm still working on it, you may
fork this repository, keep developing it and release it, as long as:
- it uses a different name and its own branding (the name "Chef Shared Loader", "Th3chef" and their logos and art
  stay mine);
- it says clearly that it's a continuation of Chef Shared Loader by Th3chef, with a link to this repository;
- it doesn't claim to be the original or an official version.

A continuation released this way may carry on under these same terms even if I release a new version later.

